{
  "Name": "Okta - Admin & Configuration Changes - Okta Admin Role Assigned to a User or Group",
  "Description": "Alert: Okta\nGroup: Admin & Configuration Changes\nMITRE ATT&CK: Persistence / T1098.003\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\nTuning: okta_user_allowlist / okta_ip_allowlist keys \"<login without domain>|Okta Admin Role Assigned to a User or Group\" or \"<ip>|Okta Admin Role Assigned to a User or Group\"\n\nDetects administrator roles being assigned in Okta: to a user (user.account.privilege.grant), to a group (group.privilege.grant), or through a custom role binding (iam.resourceset.bindings.add). New administrators are a common persistence and escalation step. Merges the separate user, group and resource-set rules.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_admin_role_assigned_to_user_or_group/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/?query=okta.yml",
  "Labels": [
    "okta",
